{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794172431,"nonce":"TwlB2j7jWpizwMoWlAzpNnGmnnA=","message":"## Design as approved (replaces the kind-and-argument design above where they differ)\n\nThe user chose a built-in over a configured kind, and the requester narrowed the values. The approved design:\n\n### Color is a built-in a type switches on (schema.md)\n- `color` becomes a fifth built-in in `schema.Builtins`, of a new kind `color` that is the built-in's alone, as `rank`'s is: `ParseKind` refuses `kind: color` on any other field.\n- Unlike the other four, it exists only on a type that switches it on: a type attribute, `color: true` in the schema document (`types: {story: {color: true, ...}}`). Absent or false, the type has no `color` field, and a write of `color` is refused as an unknown key is. \"Built-ins are code\" and \"No field roles\" are rewritten to say five built-ins and that `color` alone is per type.\n- Values are a fixed set in code, the 12 ANSI colors that read on any theme: `red`, `green`, `yellow`, `blue`, `magenta`, `cyan`, `bright-red`, `bright-green`, `bright-yellow`, `bright-blue`, `bright-magenta`, `bright-cyan`. A write of anything else is refused naming the set. Black, white and their bright forms are left out because each clashes with the background or foreground on some theme.\n- They are drawn with the terminal's own palette (SGR 31–36, 91–96; ANSI indices 1–6 and 9–14), never 256-color or truecolor, so they follow the user's theme.\n- Not a configured kind that any field may take: the gantt would then need an argument naming the field, and the point of the color is that it belongs to the issue, so every surface finds it by one key.\n\n### Stored like any field\n`git work issue set ID '{\"color\":\"blue\"}'`, `null` clears; replicated by push and pull; `issue get`/`list` read it as `fields.color`.\n\n### The gantt (views.md, \"Gantt groups are colors\")\nWith `group_by` a relation, a group whose heading issue has a `color` draws its bars and header in it; a group without one takes the palette's next color in group order as today. No argument. The grabbed bar's yellow is kept; a bar in a `yellow` group is told apart from the grab by the grab's bold.\n\n### Show\nThe fields table draws `color` as its id in its color; `Space` edits it with the enum picker over the 12 and a clear.\n\n### Jira (jira.md)\n`color` is local-only: no Jira alias is accepted on it, `jira schema` never pairs it, and a synced issue with a color reports no pending and no off-schema item for it.","files":null}]}